# The pace of the advance on each segment of the front (war window)
war-segment-pace = Advance: ours { $ours }; theirs { $theirs }.
war-segment-pace-tip = A second-generation army moves at the pace of its mobile troops (cavalry, lorries or armour) on the segment where they are at least a third of the men; elsewhere, at the pace of the infantry on foot.
war-pace-static = standing still
war-pace-foot = at the pace of the infantry on foot
war-pace-light = at the pace of the light infantry
war-pace-horse = at the pace of the cavalry
war-pace-wheeled = at the pace of the lorries
war-pace-tracked = at the pace of the armour
war-pace-ship = at the pace of the ships
war-pace-aircraft = at the pace of the aircraft
war-pace-share = { $pace } ({ $share } of the men)
war-segment-even = The men at the front are shared out evenly among the segments, so segments of the same terrain repeat the numbers.
